Third-party data
----------------
Aberystwyth Leaf Evaluation Dataset (ALED)
  Bell, J. and Dee, H. M. (2016). Aberystwyth Leaf Evaluation Dataset.
  Aberystwyth University / National Plant Phenomics Centre. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.168158
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  Changes made by CERES:
  - Frames are subsampled (about one per 2 h of imaging), downscaled to 1024 px, and re-encoded as JPEG.
  - The demo bundle (data/demo/frames/, 844 files, and the canopy masks in data/demo/seed.db.gz) contains these
    frames downscaled again to 640 px wide and re-encoded as JPEG (quality 65), so the offline demo runs without the
    original dataset. For trays B and C after their fault start the bundled frames are the altered versions below.
    The 61.6 GB original archive and the full-resolution frames are not redistributed.
  - From each tray's configured fault start, frames of tray B are altered by a deterministic image transform
    (plants shrunk and colour-dulled to simulate wilting), and frames of tray C are time-warped and dimmed (to
    simulate low light). These altered frames are generated locally and labelled "SIMULATED FAULT" everywhere in
    the app. ALED itself contains no stress treatments.

Attribution: the images were created by Bell and Dee (Aberystwyth University / National Plant Phenomics Centre) and
are shared under CC BY 4.0; CERES is not endorsed by the authors. Changes are indicated above.

Third-party software and models
-------------------------------
meta-sam-parser (PyPI): used as an installed dependency to parse sam-3.1 output. It is not vendored or
redistributed in this repository. It is licensed under the SAM License (https://github.com/meta-models/meta-sam).
Results produced with SAM: this project uses SAM 3.1 via the Meta Model API to segment plant images.

Meta Model API (muse-spark-1.3, muse-spark-1.3-contributor, sam-3.1): accessed as a hosted service under Meta's
terms for the Meta Model API (https://dev.meta.ai). No model weights are included in this repository.

Other open-source dependencies and their licences are listed in HACKATHON.md.
